# The environment an aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu build of this workspace needs on a machine
# that setup-arm64-cross.sh has set up. One copy of six variables, read two ways: a build
# machine sources it (set -a; . arm64-cross.env; set +a), and the CI arm64 job appends it
# to $GITHUB_ENV. Plain KEY=value lines only — no `export` — because that is the shape
# both readers accept. A linker only CI knows about is how two builds of "the same" commit
# come out different.
#
# What the variables are for: cargo is told which linker to use for the target, because it
# will not guess aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc; build scripts that compile C (openssl-sys and
# friends, through the cc crate) are told which cross compiler to compile it with; and
# pkg-config, which refuses to work for a foreign target by default, is told the refusal
# does not apply and where the arm64 .pc files live. PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR=/ makes
# pkg-config's sysroot prefixing a no-op: the arm64 libraries are installed under
# /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu on this machine, not inside a sysroot directory.
CARGO_TARGET_AARCH64_UNKNOWN_LINUX_GNU_LINKER=aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc
CC_aarch64_unknown_linux_gnu=aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc
CXX_aarch64_unknown_linux_gnu=aarch64-linux-gnu-g++
PKG_CONFIG_ALLOW_CROSS=1
PKG_CONFIG_PATH=/usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/pkgconfig:/usr/share/pkgconfig
PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR=/
